4.1 The obligations established under Clause 3 shall not apply to any element of information in respect of which the Receiving Party is able to demonstrate conclusively by contemporaneous written documentation that such information:
4.1.1 was already lawfully within the public domain prior to the time of its disclosure by the Disclosing Party, or subsequently entered the public domain through publication, open distribution or otherwise, without any direct or indirect breach, fault, negligence or omission on the part of the Receiving Party or its personnel;
4.1.2 was already lawfully in the possession of the Receiving Party prior to its transmission under this Agreement, without any duty of secrecy or restriction on use;
4.1.3 was lawfully obtained after the Effective Date from a bona fide third party who had the legitimate right to disclose such information without being subject to any direct or indirect obligation of confidentiality owed towards the Disclosing Party; or
4.1.4 was conceived, authored and independently developed by employees or collaborators of the Receiving Party without having had access to, knowledge of, or reference to the Disclosing Party's Confidential Information.

